issues.problem:
**E-S2.13's attack figures never run the loop they were built to stress.** The cost bullet's attacks take 19.0–30.1 ms. Fixer F's summary says they were "built to stress the loop". They do not reach it.
- Every one of them crosses gaps 0.0105 across. There the part across holds each probe at once, so held never walks the set.
- The 19 rods' boxes sit over the crossings but are never asked.

**Where the walk does run** (my work/advwin.luau and advab.luau): the gaps lie 0.01200015 across, inside (HIDE_OFFSET + EPS_GEOM, REACH]. The part across misses each probe by 1.5e-7, so every test walks the set. Against r3, 9 rounds alternating, 15–23 % busy:
- 12 Blade plates turned 30° about Y: 37.4 ms against 30.8 (×1.215);
- turned 60°: ×1.063;
- 21 plates: ×1.081;
- 12 plates turned ±60° in turn: ×1.021–1.138, and one of them plays Hammering 0.5733 → 0.5911.

The longest stretches are 0.17–0.28 ms; worst valid 8 takes 64.8 ms in the same process. So the cost is bounded and charged, and the gate holds; but the quoted attacks are not the loop's cost.

